# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000086  -  CAT II
# The web server must protect system resources and privileged operations
# from hosted applications.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000086
group:           V-206384
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk bounds what an app's searches and endpoints may reach: a role
                 declares the indexes its searches are allowed to run against, and each
                 REST endpoint declares the capability the session user must hold before it
                 will run.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.
governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.

check:           authorize.conf [role_<roleName>] srchIndexesAllowed non_empty
check:           restmap.conf [] capability present

external:        CPU, memory, and file system limits on the Splunk processes themselves,
                 carried by the operating system through cgroups and resource limits or by
                 the container runtime; workload_pools.conf cpu_weight and mem_weight
                 apportion only the share already granted to the daemon and depend on host
                 cgroup support (workload_pools.conf.spec:74, workload_pools.conf.spec:80).
external:        Privileged operations on the host that no Splunk setting mediates, carried
                 by the service account's own privileges and any mandatory access control
                 policy.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000086 check and fix text;
                 authorize.conf.spec:292 (srchIndexesAllowed), restmap.conf.spec:111
                 (capability = <capabilityName>), workload_pools.conf.spec:74
finding:         Roles do not declare the indexes their searches may reach, or REST
                 endpoints do not declare a required capability, so the application does
                 not confine a hosted app's searches and endpoints to the resources it
                 needs.
